      "chapter": "global",
      "anchor": "global-minor-dimension",
      "title": "The number of independent columns of one word",
      "statement": "The minor-list contribution and the residual diagonal estimate give dim ker Aᵤ ≤ e₀dᵤ and rank Aᵤ ≥ (1−e₀)dᵤ, with e₀ = 2 exp(−kf log k) + 2C₀/Γ.",
      "hypotheses": "One chosen word with positive normalization; its full dᵤ-dimensional source; the two diagonal subseries estimates, positive Γ and D∗, and the size proviso dᵤΓ²/D∗ ≤ C₀.",
      "correspondence": "The pinned diagonal theorem supplies the squared Hilbert–Schmidt budget. The rank and nullity inequalities are deductions proved here. The family proof explicitly uses the weaker consequence Dall > 0 when e₀ < 1 and dᵤ > 0.",
