    {
      "id": "MDR-02",
      "chapter": "global",
      "anchor": "global-minor-frame-rank",
      "title": "The joint span occupies at least D/(1+5σ) dimensions",
      "statement": "The two Gram estimates imply tr F ≥ (1−√e₀)R and tr(F²) ≤ (1+η₀)R²/D∗ + (1+√e₀)²R. Together with D ≤ (1+η₁)D∗ these imply rank F ≥ D/(1+5σ).",
      "hypotheses": "A finite family of normalized column maps between finite-dimensional complex inner-product spaces. D∗ > 0, R ≥ D∗/σ, 0 < σ ≤ 1/4, −1 ≤ η₀, e₀ ≥ 0, and η₀, η₁, √e₀ ≤ σ/2. The distinct-word, diagonal and independent row bounds all hold.",
      "correspondence": "The source combines the two moments with the independent row inequality. The displayed rank consequence follows by Cauchy–Schwarz on the positive eigenvalues and the equality between the range of F and the span of all columns.",
